@page "/docs/components/checkbox"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Checkbox
<PageTitle>Checkbox - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Checkbox</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="checkbox" />
        </div>
        <p>A tri-state checkbox: besides checked and unchecked, <code>CheckedState.Indeterminate</code> draws a minus and reports <code>aria-checked="mixed"</code> to screen readers. It renders a <code>&lt;button role="checkbox"&gt;</code> with an enlarged touch target, and its state flows through <code>@@bind-Checked</code> rather than a hidden form input.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(CheckboxDefaultExample)" Description="Give the checkbox an `id` and point a `BzLabel` at it with `For`. The label then names the checkbox for screen readers." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Description="Because the label is linked through `For`, clicking its text toggles the box as well." Example="typeof(CheckboxDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="States" Description="The three values of `CheckedState`. Indeterminate shows a minus, which suits a parent checkbox whose children are only partly selected." Example="typeof(CheckboxStatesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Status colors" Description="Set `Color` to a `StatusColor` to paint the checked fill with that status token instead of the primary color." Example="typeof(CheckboxColorsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled" Example="typeof(CheckboxDisabledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Controlled" Description="Bind `Checked` two-way to a `CheckedState` field. The button in this example shows that your code can set the indeterminate state too." Example="typeof(CheckboxControlledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="`Class` accepts `data-checked:` utilities, which apply only while the box is checked. This example uses them for round boxes with custom fills."
          Example="typeof(CheckboxCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the box moves to the right of its label." Example="typeof(CheckboxRtlExample)" />
</div>

